# The desktop user administers this machine (`bootc upgrade`, system units, setting the
# password sshd requires).
#
# NOPASSWD: tty1 and tty2 autologin, so anyone at the keyboard already has this shell; a
# sudo prompt would stop only the user, and with no password shipped it is unanswerable,
# leaving no route to root. sshd refusing an empty password holds the network boundary.
%wheel ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
